<title>USA: Fix-Corp to buy 51 pct Fix-Sports stake.</title>
<headline>Fix-Corp to buy 51 pct Fix-Sports stake.</headline>
<dateline>BEACHWOOD, Ohio 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fix-Corp International Inc said on Monday it agreed to buy a 51 percent stake in Fix-Sports Inc, an Ohio-based athletic shoe marketing and sales company, for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The specialized factory company said in a statement Fix-Sports had the potential to generate between $5 million and $10 million in revenues in its first year.</p>
<p>President and Chief Executive Officer Mark Fixler told Reuters the purchase would be made via a stock option plan and that Fix-Sports was part of Steele's Holding Co, a softball equipment supplier.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
